# Sector index definitions (plan.md §19 Part 1). Operator-editable data.
#
# One JSON object per line:
#   {"ticker": "MIN", "name": "Minerals & Ore",
#    "roots": [1857, 1031], "min_members": 8, "min_unit_volume": 1000}
#
# `roots` are marketGroup ids whose SUBTREES define membership; a type belongs
# to the sector if any root is an ancestor of its market group. Members come
# from the tracked universe only, and NPC-price-seeded items are excluded.
#
# `min_members` — below this the sector renders UNKNOWN rather than being
# merged into a neighbour or shown as a thin index nobody should trust.
# `min_unit_volume` — optional per-sector floor (some industries are
# structurally thinner than the market-wide default); omit to inherit
# `config.toml`'s universe floor. Each sector's floor and resulting member
# count render in its diagnostics.
#
# The market-group ids below were read from the live SDE on 2026-08-20.
